.TH DOCKER-HELPER 1
.SH NAME
docker-helper \- Policy-enforcing Docker mediation daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B docker-helper
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.BI "COMMAND"
[\& ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B docker-helper
is a policy-enforcing daemon that provides a restricted interface to Docker.
It mediates Docker operations for coding agents running on the same machine,
restricting host path access to session workspaces and enforcing policy on
build, pull, and run operations.
.PP
Deployment mode is determined by effective UID:
.IP \(bu 4
\fIUser mode\fR (non-root): Private Unix socket, per-user configuration
.IP \(bu 4
\fISystem mode\fR (root): System Unix socket + loopback HTTP, system-wide configuration
.SH DEPLOYMENT MODES
.SS User Mode
Runs as the current user. Configuration at
.IR ~/.config/docker-helper/config.json ,
state at
.IR ~/.local/state/docker-helper .
No AppArmor integration.
.SS System Mode
Runs as root. Configuration at
.IR /etc/docker-helper/config.json ,
state at
.IR /var/lib/docker-helper .
AppArmor confinement with managed workspace roots.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS General Commands
.TP
.B docker-helper serve
Start the HTTP server (daemon mode).
.TP
.B docker-helper init [\-\-allowed-root PATH]
Initialize configuration and admin token. In system mode, the initial
allowed_root is added to managed AppArmor roots. Subsequent changes to
configuration or principal allowed roots do NOT automatically update AppArmor;
use \fIdocker-helper apparmor root\fR to manage them.
.TP
.B docker-helper reload [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE]
Reload configuration.
.TP
.B docker-helper version
Print version information.
.TP
.B docker-helper help [COMMAND]
Show help for a command.
.SS Session Commands
.TP
.B docker-helper session create [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE] \-\-workspace PATH
Create a new session for a workspace.
.TP
.B docker-helper session list [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE]
List active sessions.
.TP
.B docker-helper session delete [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE] \-\-id SESSION_ID
Delete a session by ID.
.TP
.B docker-helper session cleanup
Remove expired sessions from the local state database.
.SS Config Commands
.TP
.B docker-helper config show [FIELD]
Show configuration values. Without FIELD, prints complete effective config as JSON.
.TP
.B docker-helper config set FIELD VALUE
Set a configuration value. Writable fields: allowed_root, session_ttl, log_level,
audit_enabled, shutdown_timeout, operation_retention_ttl, operation_max_completed,
operation_log_max_bytes, trusted_ca_path, trusted_ca_injection, http_address.
.TP
.B docker-helper config unset FIELD
Unset a configuration value. Unsettable fields: log_level, audit_enabled,
shutdown_timeout, operation_retention_ttl, operation_max_completed,
operation_log_max_bytes, trusted_ca_path, trusted_ca_injection, http_address.
.SS Principal Commands
.TP
.B docker-helper principal create [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE] USER
Create a new principal.
.TP
.B docker-helper principal list [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE] [\-\-json]
List all principals (username, UID, GID, home, enabled).
.TP
.B docker-helper principal show [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE] USER [FIELD]
Show principal details.
.TP
.B docker-helper principal set [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE] USER FIELD VALUE
Modify principal settings.
.TP
.B docker-helper principal allowed-root add [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE] USER PATH
Add an allowed root for a principal.
.TP
.B docker-helper principal allowed-root remove [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE] USER PATH
Remove an allowed root from a principal.
.SS Credential Commands
.TP
.B docker-helper credential create [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE] \-\-name NAME USER
Create a new credential for a principal.
.TP
.B docker-helper credential list [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE] USER
List credentials for a principal.
.TP
.B docker-helper credential revoke [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE] CREDENTIAL_ID
Revoke a credential.
.SS Admin Commands
.TP
.B docker-helper admin token rotate [\-\-system] [\-\-endpoint ENDPOINT] [\-\-token-file FILE] [\-\-json]
Rotate the admin token. Requires the current admin token
(\fB\-\-token-file\fR is the client auth source, not the destination).
The new token is shown once on stdout; the old token is invalid
immediately and no restart is required. \fB\-\-json\fR prints the API
response.
.SS AppArmor Commands (System Mode)
.TP
.B docker-helper apparmor root list
List managed workspace roots in the AppArmor profile.
.TP
.B docker-helper apparmor root add PATH
Add a workspace root to the AppArmor profile.
.TP
.B docker-helper apparmor root remove PATH
Remove a workspace root from the AppArmor profile.
.TP
.B docker-helper apparmor check
Validate the AppArmor profile.
.SS Agent Commands
.TP
.B docker-helper pull IMAGE
Pull a Docker image.
.TP
.B docker-helper build \-\-context PATH \-\-dockerfile FILE \-\-image NAME
Build a Docker image.
.TP
.B docker-helper run \-\-image NAME [\-\-entrypoint CMD] [\-\-workdir PATH] [\-\-shm-size SIZE] \-\& [command]
Run a Docker container.
.TP
.B docker-helper registry login \-\-registry REGISTRY \-\-username USER
Log in to a container registry for the current session.
.SH OPERATOR ENDPOINT SELECTION
For reload, session, principal, and credential commands, select the target daemon:
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\-\-system\fR: Connect to system daemon (default for system mode)
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\-\-endpoint URL\fR: Explicit endpoint: \fIunix:///absolute/path\fR or \fIhttp://127.0.0.1:PORT\fR (HTTP is loopback only; requires \fB\-\-token-file\fR)
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\-\-token-file FILE\fR: Read authentication token from file
.PP
\fB\-\-system\fR and \fB\-\-endpoint\fR are mutually exclusive.
\fB\-\-endpoint\fR requires \fB\-\-token-file\fR.
\fB\-\-system\fR may use \fB\-\-token-file\fR for authentication.
Without explicit endpoint selection, a deterministic default is used.
No fallback occurs after connection failure.
.PP
Local system mode uses Unix socket + loopback HTTP (127.0.0.1:52375 default).
No remote or TLS support in Release 2.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Generic operational or runtime failure
.TP
.B 2
Invalid CLI arguments or input (where applicable)
.PP
\fBdocker-helper run\fR returns the container exit code when the container
exits with a non-zero status.
.PP
SIGINT for async build/run operations returns 130.
SIGTERM for async build/run operations returns 143.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/docker-helper/config.json
System mode configuration
.TP
.B /etc/docker-helper/admin.token
System mode admin token
.TP
.B /var/lib/docker-helper/docker-helper.db
System mode state database
.TP
.B /run/docker-helper/docker-helper.sock
System mode Unix socket
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docker-helper/config.json
User mode configuration
.TP
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/docker-helper
User mode state directory
.TP
.B dirname(config_path)/admin.token
Admin token (same directory as config)
.SH SECURITY
.IP \(bu 4
.B docker-helper
mediates Docker access; rootful Docker access is root-equivalent host capability
.IP \(bu 4
Credentials and session tokens are capabilities—protect them accordingly
.IP \(bu 4
AppArmor confinement restricts filesystem and capability access
.IP \(bu 4
No remote or non-loopback network access in Release 2
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker-helper-config (5),
.BR apparmor (7),
.BR docker-helper help COMMAND,
.BR docker-helper COMMAND \-\-help
